      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have been really excited for this Avatar scale parameter as I wanted to let others use a remote or ray gun or other fun gimmicks to write to the scale parameter to find that it’s only possible if you have a steam vr plugin and a program running and pay for it. That’s cool but I thought this was intended to do that from the beginning. I wouldn’t care if it was buggy or a bit destined, I would really enjoy being able to both read and write any one of the avatar scaling parameters. I don’t see any reason not to since scale limits are a thing now and worlds can block scaling entirely if they choose. It’s not like outsiders can write to your parameters unless you specifically choose to do that. Maybe this can be limited to private avatars or a setting users must enable., but please!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
